    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>FrontPup allows you to maximize the settings available between the CloudFront Origin and your WordPress site.</p>\n<p>Features include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Set no-cache headers for all pages (great for development or testing)</li>\n<li>Set public Cache-Control headers for CloudFront and Browsers</li>\n<li>Set private Cache-Control headers for Browsers only</li>\n<li>Set separate max-age and s-maxage values</li>\n</ul>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id='do%20i%20need%20an%20aws%20cloudfront%20to%20use%20this%20plugin%3F'>\nDo I need an AWS CloudFront to use this plugin?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes, you need an AWS account with CloudFront setup for your website.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>First version of this plugin</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Your CloudFront companion.",
    "description": "<p>FrontPup allows you to maximize the settings available between the CloudFront Origin and your WordPress site.</p>\n<p>Features include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Set no-cache headers for all pages (great for development or testing)</li>\n<li>Set public Cache-Control headers for CloudFront and Browsers</li>\n<li>Set private Cache-Control headers for Browsers only</li>\n<li>Set separate max-age and s-maxage values</li>\n</ul>\n",
